# Storefront — production build settings.
#
# Vite loads this automatically for `npm run build` and inlines the values at
# build time, so a rebuild is what changes them. Nothing here is a secret:
# everything in a VITE_* variable ships inside the JavaScript bundle and is
# readable by anyone who opens the shop. Never put the admin passcode, a
# database string or a payment key in one.

# Where the REST API lives.
#
# The /api suffix is part of it — the client asks for paths like /bootstrap and
# /products, and this is what they hang off. Leaving it off means every request
# goes to https://api.skvpyros.in/products and 404s.
#
# Unset, the client falls back to a same-origin /api, which is what the dev
# server proxies. That fallback is also the better production setup if the shop
# and the API ever share a domain: a reverse-proxy rule sending /api to the API
# avoids cross-origin requests altogether, and with them CORS and the
# mixed-content rule below.
VITE_API_URL=https://api.skvpyros.in/api

# The API must be reachable over HTTPS. A page served over HTTPS may not fetch
# over plain HTTP — the browser blocks it as mixed content, silently as far as
# the shop is concerned, and every product request fails. It is not enough for
# http:// to redirect to https://: the block happens before the request is sent.
